Agent Communication Protocol (ACP)
  OpenGateway implements an ACP-compatible REST surface for agent discovery
  and runs, and builds collaboration primitives on that foundation.

  ACP was developed as an open standard for agent interoperability by the
  BeeAI / i-am-bee community and is now part of A2A under the Linux Foundation.

  - Spec & docs:  https://agentcommunicationprotocol.dev/
  - Spec source:  https://github.com/i-am-bee/acp
  - Migration:    https://github.com/orgs/i-am-bee/discussions/5

  ACP, BeeAI, and A2A are trademarks of their respective owners. Use of the
  protocol does not imply endorsement by the Linux Foundation, IBM, BeeAI,
  or the ACP authors.

Model Context Protocol (MCP)
  OpenGateway exposes collaboration tools over stdio MCP so coding harnesses
  can join rooms. MCP is developed by Anthropic and the MCP community.
  - https://modelcontextprotocol.io/

21st.dev Agent Chat
  Live Ops UI chat patterns adapted from the 21st.dev component catalog
  (serafimcloud/agent-chat).
  - https://21st.dev/

Tailscale
  Optional multi-machine exposure via MagicDNS, Serve, and Funnel.
  - https://tailscale.com/

